# PATCH: 021-citrix-capture-protection
#
# Windows browser builds running in an ICA session require a verified endpoint
# capture-protection lease before browser UI is created. The primary process
# opens the DENCAP static virtual channel through the VDA WFAPI runtime, sends
# ACQUIRE/RENEW/RELEASE frames, and validates the endpoint WDA read-back.
#
# Startup fails closed when no endpoint acknowledgement is available. After an
# established 30-second lease, uncertain transport failures are retried with
# fresh sequence numbers; explicit protection failures terminate immediately,
# while a separate watchdog terminates before an unrenewed lease can expire.
# Local and ordinary RDP sessions are unchanged; patch 001 continues to protect
# DenBrowser-owned HWNDs there.
#
# This patch is only the VDA sender. It requires the separately deployed signed
# Citrix Workspace virtual-driver module and VDA custom-channel allow-list entry
# documented in citrix/README.md. WDA is best-effort public-capture protection,
# not DRM, and the endpoint module must first prove that its process owns the
# top-level ICA HWND.


diff --git a/toolkit/xre/DenCitrixCaptureProtection.cpp b/toolkit/xre/DenCitrixCaptureProtection.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9aec157
--- /dev/null
+++ b/toolkit/xre/DenCitrixCaptureProtection.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,756 @@
